Mahfuz Sayem, a prospective graduate student with a strong background in Environmental Science and experience in GeoAI and machine learning, reached out to Dr. James Rising regarding admission to a research-based master's or Ph.D. program starting Fall 2027 or Spring 2028. He detailed his current research, which includes accepted abstracts on spatially validated frameworks for environmental vulnerability and vegetation dynamics analysis. Dr. Rising acknowledged the relevance of Mahfuz's experience but informed him that there is no current funding available for new graduate students and that future opportunities remain uncertain. He advised Mahfuz to keep an eye on the University of Delaware's graduate admissions and funding announcements as they become available.
